# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# Vercel does not read .gitignore, so anything excluded there has to be
# excluded again here or it rides along in the deployment tarball.

# The Windows desktop app's build output and dependencies — but NOT its source.
#
# Without these the upload was 351MB and the deploy failed outright: dist/
# holds two 80MB installers plus an unpacked build, and node_modules/electron
# ships its own ~180MB Chromium. Vercel rejects any single file over 100MB and
# electron.exe is over it.
#
# Ignoring all of `desktop/` was the obvious next move and broke the build
# instead: scripts/verify-desktop-runner.ts imports ../desktop/runner, and
# `next build` typechecks the whole project. The source is ten small files —
# it costs nothing to upload and keeps that import resolvable.
#
# The installer reaches customers through Vercel Blob, not this deployment —
# see desktop/README.md, "Publishing it so customers can download".
desktop/node_modules/
desktop/dist/

# Build output and local scratch.
.next/
out/
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.playwright-mcp/

# Packaged extension artifacts, built by scripts/package-extension.ts.
followthroo-linkedin-*.zip
